From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:55:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] thermal: apple-pmp: keep the zone when every die
 record is dark

When a CPU cluster may power down in WFI, the PMP marks its die records
invalid while the cluster is off, and with all of them dark a sample
fails with -ENODATA. apple_pmp_get_temp() passed that error to the
thermal core, which counts any error other than -EAGAIN as a broken
sensor: thermal_zone_recheck() grows its delay on every failed update,
and the 100 ms governor updates of the poll worker reach the limit
within about two seconds. thermal_zone_broken_disable() then disables
the zone, including its critical trip. With the zone disabled, the guard
holds the minimum CPU caps and the rail telemetry reads -EAGAIN for the
rest of the boot, even after the records are valid again.

On a J604 with the P cluster's power-gate enable set at runtime, the
zone was disabled 1.9 s after the write ("Unable to get temperature,
disabling!", "Disabled thermal zone with critical trip point"). CPU 7
then stayed at its minimum frequency under load, with every record
valid.

Report the dark state as -EAGAIN, so that the core checks again at its
fixed delay and keeps the zone. The guard still fails closed on the same
sample, and the shutdown on three samples of 120 C or more still runs
from the poll worker. Other errors are passed through as before.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/thermal/apple-pmp-thermal.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/thermal/apple-pmp-thermal.c b/drivers/thermal/apple-pmp-thermal.c
index ff6fb632d8..e504750a27 100644
--- a/drivers/thermal/apple-pmp-thermal.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/apple-pmp-thermal.c
@@ -508,6 +508,15 @@ static int apple_pmp_get_temp(struct thermal_zone_device *zone, int *temp)
 	if (!pmp_thermal.cooling.last_ns ||
 	    ktime_get_ns() - pmp_thermal.cooling.last_ns > 500000000ULL)
 		return -EAGAIN;
+	/*
+	 * Every die record dark is the firmware's state of a powered-down
+	 * cluster, not a broken zone. Any other error, repeated, makes the
+	 * thermal core disable the zone and its critical trip for the rest of
+	 * the boot; -EAGAIN makes it check again at its fixed delay. The guard
+	 * fails closed on the same sample either way.
+	 */
+	if (pmp_thermal.cached_error == -ENODATA)
+		return -EAGAIN;
 	if (pmp_thermal.cached_error)
 		return pmp_thermal.cached_error;
 	*temp = pmp_thermal.cached_mc;
